  "solution": "The logic followed here is : **(2nd number + 3rd number) × 4 = 1st number**\n\nGiven :\n\n__\n \n• (452, 50, 63)\n\n​**(50 + 63)**__ × 4 = 452\n\n__**113 × 4**__ = 452\n\n452 = 452 (LHS = RHS)\n\n__\n \n• (260, 35, 30)​\n\n​**(35**** + 30**__) × 4 = 260\n\n__65 × 4__ = 260\n\n260 = 260 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n__\n \n• Option - (1) : (330, 30, 45)​\n\n​(30 + 45__) × 4 = 330\n\n__75 × 4__ = 330\n\n**300 ≠ 330 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n__\n \n• Option - (2) : (260, 30, 25)​\n\n​(30 + 25__) × 4 = 260\n\n__55 × 4__ = 260\n\n**220 ≠ 260 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n__\n \n• Option - (3) : (260, 50, 15)​\n\n​(50 + 15__) × 4 = 260\n\n__65 × 4__ = 260\n\n**260 = 260 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n__\n \n• Option - (4) : (230, 15, 45)\n\n​(15 + 45__) × 4 = 230\n\n__60 × 4__ = 230\n\n**240 ≠ 230 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\nHence, **\"Option - (3)\"** is the correct answer.\n\n5f:T133f,\n<p st",
